{{!--
  dreamd's desktop entry: a handlebars template, rendered by tauri-bundler.

  Pointed at by `bundle.linux.deb.desktopTemplate`, but it is not deb-only — the
  AppImage's AppDir is built by `debian::generate_data` into `bundle/appimage_deb`
  and the `.tar.gz` is that same staged tree, so all three Linux artifacts carry
  the entry rendered from this one file.

  It exists for the two lines the bundler's default template cannot express:

    MimeType  without it dreamd never appears under "Open With" for a markdown
              file on any desktop, which for a markdown reader is the whole
              integration. `text/markdown` is RFC 7763; `text/x-markdown` is the
              pre-RFC name still emitted by older shared-mime-info.
    %f        the field code that passes the chosen path. MimeType without it
              registers dreamd as a handler that then launches with no argument.

  `%f` and not `%F`: `Cli::path` is a single `Option<PathBuf>`, so a multi-select
  would hand clap several paths and it would refuse them. `%f` makes the launcher
  spawn one dreamd per file instead, which is the behaviour that actually works.

  This block is a *handlebars* comment, not a `#` one, so it is stripped at
  render time — the rationale stays here and never ships to /usr/share.
--}}
[Desktop Entry]
Categories={{categories}}
{{#if comment}}
Comment={{comment}}
{{/if}}
Exec={{exec}} %f
StartupWMClass={{exec}}
Icon={{icon}}
Name={{name}}
Terminal=false
Type=Application
MimeType=text/markdown;text/x-markdown;
